Lock order status to the despatch/invoicing process, invoice partial
despatches, add Delivery History, add DPD Track links (v0.104)

Order status:
- INVOICE_PENDING/COMPLETED/PARTIALLY_DESPATCHED can no longer be chosen
  manually from the Status field, on create or edit - they're set only by
  DespatchService/InvoiceService.
- Once an order is INVOICE_PENDING or COMPLETED, its status is locked -
  any other manual change is rejected - except adding/increasing order
  lines, which automatically reopens it as PARTIALLY_DESPATCHED for an
  extra shipment and resets shippingInvoiced so a new shipping
  cost/courier/service can be set in the same save.
- OrderService.update() computes this up front (statusBeforeEdit,
  wasLocked, extraStockNeeded) before reconcileLines touches anything.

Invoicing:
- InvoiceService.INVOICEABLE_STATUSES now covers PARTIALLY_DESPATCHED as
  well as INVOICE_PENDING, in both pending() and generate() - a partial
  despatch is invoiceable for exactly what's shipped so far, using the
  existing despatched-minus-invoiced quantity math.
- New OrderRepository.findByStatusInAndOrderTypeOrderByOrderDateAsc for
  the widened query.

Picking/despatch queues (found while sanity-checking the above):
- PickingService.readyToPick()/start() and DespatchService.readyToPack()
  only matched AWAITING_DESPATCH, so a reopened order (now
  PARTIALLY_DESPATCHED) would silently vanish from both queues despite
  genuinely needing picking and despatching again. Both now also match
  PARTIALLY_DESPATCHED via a new
  OrderRepository.findByStatusInAndPickingStatusInOrderByOrderDateAsc.

Delivery History (new, Sales):
- Order.despatchedAt (V49 migration) - set once on first despatch, never
  cleared by Reverse to Despatch - the stable "despatched at least once"
  marker and date basis for this page.
- DeliveryHistoryService/Controller: list (search + date range), detail
  (per-unit MAC/serial/batch/carton, handling the SERIAL-vs-SPLIT carton
  resolution difference), and Excel export at both levels (Apache POI,
  matching ReportService's pattern).
- Frontend: DeliveryHistory.tsx (list) and DeliveryHistoryDetail.tsx
  (detail), routed and added to the Sales nav group.

Tracking:
- frontend/src/utils/tracking.ts - dpdTrackingUrl() builds DPD's public
  tracking URL from a consignment number + postcode (best-effort, not
  smoke-tested against a live consignment in this environment).
- "Track" links added to OrderEdit's Despatch panel, the post-despatch
  banners in SplitPacking.tsx/SerialPacking.tsx, and each Delivery
  History detail page.

Known limitation (documented in CHANGELOG): an order reopened for an
extra shipment reuses whatever DPD shipment was already booked rather
than booking a new one, since Order only records a single DPD
shipment/consignment - a genuine second DPD booking would need the data
model to support more than one shipment per order, not built here.

CHANGELOG.md, README.md and the User Guide PDF (Sections 1.2, 1.4 new
note, new 1.5 Delivery History, 3.4) updated to match.

